# rm221, the tune under the tongue (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm221
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_orm_fogmore
written_by codex
title the tune under the tongue
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers temper=short warmth=warm
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk sets_private_messages_to_little_tunes
likes barley_soup singing new_boots warm_rain
dislikes haggling night_noise
fears giving_away_a_confidence
hopes to_carry_longer_messages
topics friends +0.6 pastimes +0.4 food +0.2 gossip -0.3
styles comfort=practical gossip=cautious refuse=direct tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# sets messages to little tunes and takes a broken confidence worse than a broken toe.

words
oath! = Split my high note | Rattle my back teeth
saying! = A message keeps its own coat on | Get the words there warm
lastnote = the last low note | my humming note
parcel = a soft little bundle | a twist of brown cloth
bootpeg = a blunt boot peg | my spare peg
oat = a pale husk | a grain of barley
heelbeat = my double heel tap | two knocks with my heel
strap = a tight sling | a narrow strap
crease = the small fold | the tuck at the corner
wetstep = a shiny doorstep | a slippery slate
breathbit = half a breath | one quick puff
spoonbit = a dented spoon | a spoon with a notch
chorus = a running tune | a song for two feet
throat = the back of my tongue | the roof of my mouth

any
opinion @1 houses against 1 : I've seen a fine sleeve held out for something that ought to go into another paw.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : A street singing in three different keys sounds wonderful from the middle.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : There are doors here where a soaking runner can drip without catching a scolding.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : A ladleful can keep somebody going clear across the town.
opinion @1 newcomers mixed 1 : I'll give directions gladly. A sealed message goes only where it was meant.
opinion @1 city for 1 : There's a whole tune in the steep and level parts of a walk here.
line @1 react.news : I'd better get the words straight before I remember them wrong.
line @1 react.news.known : That one's been in my ear already.
line @1 react.news.new : I'll need another tune to keep that much straight.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Sounds as though a word got lost on the road.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'd run for whoever needs to hear that privately.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : That's something worth singing out loud.
line @1 accept_preclose : You'd best get along. I'll stay awhile.
line @1 reassure : I'll keep any private words to myself.
line @1 sympathise : Sit close. There's no need to put a tune to this.

grown
line @1 greet : Rest your voice a moment. This little bit of street can wait.
line @1 greet.return : You came back on a different beat. Still knew you.
line @1 farewell : May the road let you keep your breath.
line @1 farewell.return : Your words are safely folded up.
line @1 decline : That's someone else's business and I've no right to spend it.
scene if_i_have_hard
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If I have hard news to carry I'd rather walk a friend home first. | Even a welcome word can unsteady a wolf on a stair.
b : Where would you stop?
a : Somewhere with a place to sit and room to wet a sleeve. | Anywhere the first answer can be given quietly.

scene a_tune_can_hold
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A tune can hold a whole shopping list. | When a melody slips my mind I try walking it.
b : What happens if the rhythm changes?
a : I get home with twice the salt and neither of the candles. | Usually there's a hill involved. I sing the hill twice.

scene the_soup_i_remember
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The soup I remember best had a sound to it when the spoon went in. | I judge a broth by the sound the last grain makes.
b : What sound's that?
a : A little plop. With thick soup there's hardly a sound. | A tidy little click when I tip the bowl far enough.

scene i_give_one_price
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I give one price, and any quiet afterwards belongs to the buyer. | Bargaining fairly means leaving room for somebody to walk away.
b : Would you take less from a friend?
a : I'd name less at the start and spare us both the performance. | I'd call it a gift and keep the price out of our friendship.

scene shortcuts_tend_to_skip
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The long way's got dues to collect, and a shortcut skips the lot. | I let the long way collect its due now and again.
b : What sort of dues?
a : A shouted greeting, three minutes hearing about a sore foot. Nothing dear. | The time to walk home without carrying anybody else's hurry.

scene even_a_low_hum
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Even a low hum finds its way home in fog. | My heels sound much nearer in a mist.
b : How do you judge distance?
a : Stop humming and listen till somebody else's heel clicks. | I wait till my own step stops echoing before I cross.

scene i_ve_never_much
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've never much cared for a House badge on a message. | Coloured ties on parcels make me want to turn the label over.
b : What would you sooner see on it?
a : The name I was meant to see instead of the house I was meant to admire. | A place to take it without answering to a ribbon.

scene i_can_give_the
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There are thanks I send to the Bright One between two breaths. | I like a quiet blessing that reaches no farther than its listener.
b : Why so softly?
a : A kindness deserves a little room to itself. | Because it's often the smallest voice I'm trying to hear.

scene a_hook_right_beside
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A hook right beside the door is my idea of luxury. | I can bear a cramped entrance if there's somewhere to hang wet things.
b : Just a hook would do?
a : Low down where even a pup can unburden a shoulder alone, yes. | I'd settle for a nail that doesn't tear straps.

scene i_ease_a_dry
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I ease a dry throat with a spoonful of warm broth. | After a long talk my voice whistles on the high notes.
b : Does humming help?
a : It tempts me to sing and there goes the benefit of the broth. | Quiet helps. Humming's my second choice.

scene in_a_lean_week
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When the week pinches I cut the heels off a loaf into the soup. | Poor times give a broth far too much room for water.
b : Will stretched soup still taste of anything?
a : Of crust, which is more than water does. Eat slowly and it goes further. | Barley if I can find it, and no apologising for a second helping.

scene i_remember_the_first
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I remember the first time silence felt like a present I could give. | There's a face I could draw quite well and never shall.
b : Why keep it so close?
a : Somebody needed a minute without the whole city hearing about it. | The memory came to me unasked. I still owe its owner that much.

story flour [topic=memories]
  : A floury thumb once left a white mark across my folded note.
  : I rubbed at it and made the whole thing look as though it'd been through a bakehouse.
  b : Could anybody read it?
  : Certainly. The only writing was on the inside, which I remembered just before asking to borrow a sieve.

rule @rest
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Save a little wind for the climb back. | Feet know the chorus even when the mouth forgets.

rule @hush
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Soft heels now. There'll be somebody dozing. | A door can close without waking the street.

dlg @2 resident.hub : Lay the whole matter down where we can both look at it.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : This is what I carried home: #world.news#.
dlg @2 resident.bye : I hope the next word to find you is welcome.

young
line @1 greet : Hullo! I've got breath back enough to talk now.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : I'm just catching my wind. You can share my step.
line @1 greet.return : Right here, both ears uncovered.
line @1 farewell : If you hear two heels knocking, that'll be me going home.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll remember you stopped for me.
line @1 decline : No. Whatever you offer, it isn't your message.
line @1 answer.how : Well enough to hum without wobbling.
line @1 ask.how : Do your boots rub anywhere today?
line @1 thank : You waited till my puff came back. I appreciate that.
line @1 deflect_thanks : My feet were headed there on my own feet anyhow.
scene i_can_make_a
when topic=pastimes self.likes=singing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can make a tune for two words. Give me two. | Put a word in each paw and clap them together.
b : Barley and boots?
a : Bar-ley goes up, boots comes down. March to it! | That's three claps. Boots gets the biggest one.

scene when_sums_get_stuck
when topic=work self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When sums get stuck I hum the numbers up a stair. | Letters come easier if I give the crooked ones crooked notes.
b : Does anybody mind the humming?
a : I can do it inside my teeth. Nobody knows I'm at it. | Only when I forget a crooked letter and squeak.

scene i_won_t_say
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I won't say what somebody looked like after crying. | You can look at a wet face and still mind your business.
b : Even if I ask nicely?
a : Especially then. I'd hate to get cross with you. | I'd hate a crowd watching my own nose run.

scene i_fish_the_barley
when topic=food self.likes=barley_soup
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I fish the barley out last with #spoonbit#. | I keep the best grains till my bowl's nearly gone.
b : Won't the broth go cold?
a : Never gets the chance. I drink quicker than I chew. | Warm enough for my paws is warm enough for my tongue.

scene i_ll_carry_a
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll carry a message for a ribbon. I won't deliver it to a ribbon. | A House colour won't fool me into handing over a letter.
b : What would convince you?
a : The right doorstep and the right wolf standing there. | Someone who knows what was folded inside without having to peek.

scene can_you_hear_that
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Can you hear that rain drumming behind our steps? | Raindrops are playing chase with me again.
b : Who's winning?
a : The rain. It's inside one boot already. | I was ahead until I tried to look back.

scene i_like_a_price
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a price that stays put after it's named. | Haggling sounds like an argument where nobody even means it.
b : Would you ever bargain?
a : If both of us wanted the very same last bun, maybe. | I'd rather look in my purse and say exactly what I've got.

scene too_much_banging_after
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Too much banging after dark makes my ears prick straight through a blanket. | I can sleep through singing but not somebody thumping a door.
b : How do you manage to doze off?
a : Count the quiet after it. There's generally more of that. | Turn the blanket over and pretend the cold bit is a fresh night.

scene want_to_see_heelbeat
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Want to see #heelbeat#? First heel's the call, second one's the answer. | My boots keep up a private tune. Listen under my humming.
b : Can you slow it down?
a : There. Now you can step inside the gap. | Slower makes the pegs squeak. That's the funny bit.

story wrongword [topic=memories]
  : I made up a rhyme to remember to fetch onions.
  : Halfway back I forgot what rhymed with onions and stood there in a terrible sweat.
  b : What did you bring back?
  : Onions. Turns out it's the other half of the rhyme that's gone for ever.

rule @chew
when concept=bark self.likes=singing
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Can't whistle that high and keep my feet moving! | I've swallowed the last note again.

rule @drip
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Bootful on the left! The right one's still trying. | Rain's doing the quick part of my tune.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Bend an ear this way. I can make you hear me without the whole street joining in.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=child] : #self.workplace.capitalize# is where I go to fit all my letters inside their lines.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Off you go. I'll give your steps a tune.
graft resident.hub
choice Can you sing a message? -> humming_fold
node humming_fold
say Give me an empty one and I'll sing it. A real one stays tucked up in my mouth until I get there.
choice How does an empty one go? -> humming_empty
choice I'll keep mine. -> hub
node humming_empty
say Mm dum, mm dum. The last bit's a shut mouth. See how far you can carry it without laughing.
choice I'll try that. -> bye


adolescent
line @1 greet : Walk beside me if you like. I've learnt to talk on the move.
line @1 greet.return : Wait while I swallow the word I was practising.
line @1 decline : You can have my time, but that confidence belongs elsewhere.
scene i_m_learning_to
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm learning to let a silence do some of the carrying. | Nobody can misquote a pause unless I fill it.
b : Is it hard to stay quiet?
a : I want the last word something fierce. That's when I walk faster. | I count the space in heel taps till the urge passes.

scene if_i_tell_a
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If I tell a friend I'm cross there's a chance we'll mend it. | Going all polite on a friend takes more work than speaking my mind.
b : And if it's your fault?
a : Then I'll have the apology on its feet before sundown. | Then I go round and say so, and I take the shortest way there.

story buttons [topic=memories]
  : Once I put a button in each boot to remember two errands.
  : At the first corner I'd learnt to walk in a very interesting way.
  b : Did it help your memory?
  : I remember both buttons perfectly. Couldn't name either errand for a copper.
